        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Béla Bartók, Johann Christoph Pepusch\n- Roles: composer, pianist, ethnomusicologist\n- Works: Rhapsody, Op. 1 (Bartók)\n- Places: Hungary, England, Germany\n\nFacts:\n- Béla Viktor János Bartók was born on 25 March 1881 and died on 26 September 1945.\n- Johann Christoph Pepusch was born in 1667 and died on 20 July 1752.\n- Johann Christoph Pepusch was a German-born composer who spent most of his working life in England.\n- Béla Bartók was a Hungarian composer, pianist, and ethnomusicologist.\n- Rhapsody, Op. 1 is a work by Béla Bartók, and the chunk identifies it with the notation “Sz. 26.”",
